The user wants:
1. Chips on the rail closer together.
2. The rail should show a set number of chips based on money you have. Don't just gray out (unaffordable); remove the chip completely when you can't afford it, and bring it back when you have enough.

Interpretation: The chip rail currently has 5 chips (1,5,25,100,500), and it grays out chips you can't afford. They want:
